WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.896
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:15.437
Unit six: Helping at Home. In this unit, you will talk about chores you help with.

4
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.230
Clean.

5
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.302
Clean means to make something not dirty.

6
00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:22.439
I clean my room on Sunday.

7
00:00:23.139 --> 00:00:25.814
Your turn. Say: Clean.

8
00:00:28.514 --> 00:00:29.271
Clean.

9
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:31.122
Wash.

10
00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:34.274
Wash means to clean something with water.

11
00:00:34.574 --> 00:00:36.376
I help wash the dishes.

12
00:00:37.076 --> 00:00:40.019
Your turn. Say: Wash.

13
00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:43.592
Wash.

14
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:45.225
Cook.

15
00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:48.679
Cook means to make food hot and ready to eat.

16
00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:50.653
My dad cooks dinner.

17
00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:53.785
Your turn. Say: Cook.

18
00:00:56.485 --> 00:00:57.138
Cook.

19
00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.093
Tidy.

20
00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.315
Tidy means to put things in the right place.

21
00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:04.185
Please tidy your toys.

22
00:01:04.885 --> 00:01:07.468
Your turn. Say: Tidy.

23
00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:10.937
Tidy.

24
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.789
Chore.

25
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:15.906
Chore means a small job you do at home.

26
00:01:16.206 --> 00:01:17.799
Sweeping is my chore.

27
00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:21.024
Your turn. Say: Chore.

28
00:01:23.724 --> 00:01:24.423
Chore.

29
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:26.104
Help.

30
00:01:26.804 --> 00:01:29.257
Help means to do something for someone.

31
00:01:29.557 --> 00:01:31.440
I help my mum every day.

32
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.909
Your turn. Say: Help.

33
00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:38.238
Help.

34
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.309
Responsible.

35
00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:44.576
Responsible means doing your jobs well without being told.

36
00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:46.736
Rithy is very responsible.

37
00:01:47.436 --> 00:01:50.460
Your turn. Say: Responsible.

38
00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.301
Responsible.

39
00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:56.167
Family.

40
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:00.852
Family means your parents, brothers, sisters and relatives.

41
00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:03.047
My family eats together.

42
00:02:03.747 --> 00:02:06.631
Your turn. Say: Family.

43
00:02:09.331 --> 00:02:10.181
Family.

44
00:02:11.183 --> 00:02:13.369
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.669 --> 00:02:15.471
Rithy, do you help at home?

46
00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:19.157
Yes! I help clean the house.

47
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.368
What other chores do you do?

48
00:02:23.683 --> 00:02:26.647
I tidy my room, and I help wash the dishes.

49
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.462
Do you help cook too?

50
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.727
Sometimes. I help my mum cook rice.

51
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:38.038
Grammar focus: I help plus verb.

52
00:02:38.338 --> 00:02:40.665
I help clean. I help cook.

53
00:02:40.965 --> 00:02:48.749
After 'help', use the verb without 'to': I help cook. Add -s with he or she: she helps.

54
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.333
Now read and listen. A Helping Hand.

55
00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:55.131
I help my family at home every day.

56
00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:59.275
In the morning, I tidy my bed and my toys.

57
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:03.477
After dinner, I help wash the dishes.

58
00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:08.629
On Sunday, I help my mum clean the house and cook lunch.

59
00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:12.253
Doing chores makes me feel responsible.

60
00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.318
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:16.618 --> 00:03:18.363
I help blank the dishes.

62
00:03:18.663 --> 00:03:22.095
A, wash. B, washes. C, washed.

63
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:28.245
The answer is A: wash.

64
00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.924
A small job at home is a blank.

65
00:03:32.224 --> 00:03:35.471
A, chore. B, family. C, game.

66
00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:41.959
The answer is A: chore.

67
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.962
She blank cook dinner.

68
00:03:45.262 --> 00:03:50.645
A, help. B, helps. C, helping.

69
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.812
The answer is B: helps.

70
00:03:58.317 --> 00:04:01.828
Now it's your turn to speak. What chore do you help with at home?

71
00:04:07.128 --> 00:04:11.264
I help wash the dishes after dinner, and I tidy my room every morning.

72
00:04:11.564 --> 00:04:13.354
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:19.255
Great work today! You learned eight new words and i help plus verb.

74
00:04:19.555 --> 00:04:24.076
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

75
00:04:24.376 --> 00:04:26.727
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.027 --> 00:04:29.934
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

